IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `feg-employee`

-- Fair Entitlements Guarantee Act 2012 s 5 ("maximum weekly wage") -- the maximum weekly wage for the year my employment
-- ended, worked out under the Fair Entitlements Guarantee (Indexation of Maximum Weekly Wage) Regulations 2023, and my advance
-- with that figure in place of the input. A module beside feg-employee.l4 in the same baseline; it IMPORTs that module and
-- changes none of it.
--
-- SEAT: the employee of an insolvent employer -- "My employment ended on this day. What is the maximum weekly wage that caps my
-- advance, and how much is my advance?"
--
-- Sources:
--   the Act, Compilation No. 5 (C2025C00164), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2012A00159.txt, s 5;
--   the Regulations, F2023L00381 (made 30 March 2023, commenced 31 March 2023), as deposited at
--   ../../../fair-entitlements-guarantee-indexation-of-maximum-weekly-wage-regulations-2023/registers/source-bundle/F2023L00381.txt, s 6;
--   the Australian Statistician's estimates the Regulations index by: Average Weekly Earnings, Australia, the November 2021 to
--   November 2025 releases, deposited beside the Regulations as abs-awe-nov-2021.txt ... abs-awe-nov-2025.txt.
--
-- The Fair Entitlements Guarantee Regulations 2012 named in REQ-0088 are not the instrument that indexes: the indexation was
-- in the Fair Entitlements Guarantee (Indexation of Maximum Weekly Wage) Regulation 2013 (F2013L01439), repealed by the 2023
-- Regulations, which fix 2022-23 at $2,585 and index from there (NOTES.md finding 13).

§ `Fair Entitlements Guarantee Act 2012 s 5 -- the maximum weekly wage for my year`

-- s 5: "maximum weekly wage: the maximum weekly wage is: (a) $2,364.00; or (b) the result of indexation of the amount in
-- paragraph (a), or of the result of the last application of this paragraph, in accordance with the regulations, by reference
-- to estimates of full-time adult average weekly ordinary time earnings published by the Australian Statistician."
-- Regulations s 6(2): "The maximum weekly wage for the year starting on 1 July 2022 is $2,585." s 6(3): for "a year starting on
-- 1 July 2023, or a later year starting on 1 July", the previous year's figure, indexed by Steps 1 to 3 (below).
-- s 7: the repeal of the 2013 Regulation "does not affect the indexation, in accordance with that instrument before its repeal"
-- -- the figures for 2013-14 to 2021-22 were worked out under it, and it is not deposited: `not covered`.
DECLARE `The maximum weekly wage for my year` IS ONE OF
    `the maximum weekly wage is` HAS `the weekly dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: the year 2013-14 to 2021-22 was indexed under the repealed Fair Entitlements Guarantee (Indexation of Maximum Weekly Wage) Regulation 2013, which is not deposited`
    `not covered: the year starts before 1 July 2012, before the Act's $2,364`
    `not covered: the year starts on or after 1 July 2027, and the Australian Statistician's estimate published before that 1 July is not deposited`

-- Step 1 and Step 2's figure for a year: "the last assessment of current average weekly ordinary time earnings published by the
-- Australian Statistician before 1 July of the year". The estimates are published twice a year (the November figure in
-- February, the May figure in August), so the last one before 1 July is the previous November's. The figures, as deposited:
--   before 1 July 2022: November 2021, released 24 February 2022 -- $1,748.40
--   before 1 July 2023: November 2022, released 23 February 2023 -- $1,807.70
--   before 1 July 2024: November 2023, released 22 February 2024 -- $1,888.80
--   before 1 July 2025: November 2024, released 20 February 2025 -- $1,975.80
--   before 1 July 2026: November 2025, released 26 February 2026 -- $2,051.10
-- (each the "Seasonally Adjusted" full-time adult AWOTE row, which the releases mark "(a) This component is not seasonally
-- adjusted": the same figure as the original series; NOTES.md finding 14).
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the AWOTE estimate last published before 1 July of` MEANS
    IF `the year` EQUALS 2022 THEN 1748.40
    ELSE IF `the year` EQUALS 2023 THEN 1807.70
         ELSE IF `the year` EQUALS 2024 THEN 1888.80
              ELSE IF `the year` EQUALS 2025 THEN 1975.80
                   ELSE 2051.10

-- Step 3: "Round the result to 3 decimal places. If the fourth decimal place is 5 or above, round it up. If the rounded result
-- is less than 1, the rounded result becomes 1."
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the indexation factor for` MEANS
    max 1 ((FLOOR ((`the ratio` TIMES 1000) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 1000)
    WHERE
        `the ratio` MEANS `the AWOTE estimate last published before 1 July of` `the year` DIVIDED BY `the AWOTE estimate last published before 1 July of` (`the year` MINUS 1)

-- Step 3, continued: "Multiply the maximum weekly wage for the previous year by the rounded result. If the result includes a
-- number of cents, round the result to the nearest dollar. Round up an amount of 50 cents."
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the indexed maximum weekly wage for the year starting 1 July` MEANS
    IF `the year` AT MOST 2022
    THEN 2585
    ELSE FLOOR (((`the indexed maximum weekly wage for the year starting 1 July` (`the year` MINUS 1)) TIMES (`the indexation factor for` `the year`)) PLUS 0.5)

@export What is the Fair Entitlements Guarantee maximum weekly wage for the financial year starting on 1 July of a given year?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year starts (for example 2025 for the year 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026)
GIVETH A `The maximum weekly wage for my year`
`What is the maximum weekly wage for the year starting 1 July` MEANS
    IF `the year` LESS THAN 2012
    THEN `not covered: the year starts before 1 July 2012, before the Act's $2,364`
    ELSE IF `the year` EQUALS 2012
         THEN `the maximum weekly wage is` 2364
         ELSE IF `the year` LESS THAN 2022
              THEN `not covered: the year 2013-14 to 2021-22 was indexed under the repealed Fair Entitlements Guarantee (Indexation of Maximum Weekly Wage) Regulation 2013, which is not deposited`
              ELSE IF `the year` GREATER THAN 2026
                   THEN `not covered: the year starts on or after 1 July 2027, and the Australian Statistician's estimate published before that 1 July is not deposited`
                   ELSE `the maximum weekly wage is` (`the indexed maximum weekly wage for the year starting 1 July` `the year`)

-- ss 26(1), 27(2): the cap is "the maximum weekly wage rate at the end of the employment" (and, for wages, "at the end of that
-- period"; the wages entitlement period ends at or before the end of the employment, and the encoding takes the year of the
-- end of the employment for both -- NOTES.md finding 15).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year starting 1 July in which falls` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` AT LEAST 7
    THEN DATE_YEAR `the day`
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS 1

@export My employment with my insolvent employer ended on this day. What maximum weekly wage caps my Fair Entitlements Guarantee advance?
GIVEN `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment with the insolvent employer ended
GIVETH A `The maximum weekly wage for my year`
`What maximum weekly wage caps my advance` MEANS
    `What is the maximum weekly wage for the year starting 1 July` (`the year starting 1 July in which falls` `the day my employment ended`)

§§ `Part 3 -- how much is my advance, with the maximum weekly wage worked out`

DECLARE `My advance with the maximum weekly wage worked out` IS ONE OF
    `my advance is` HAS `the advance in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: employment for a partnership by two or more of the partners is not encoded (s 10(2))`
    `not covered: the maximum weekly wage for the year my employment ended is not worked out here`

@export How much is my Fair Entitlements Guarantee advance, with the maximum weekly wage for the year my employment ended worked out under the Regulations?
GIVEN `I was employed for a partnership by two or more partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer was a partnership, with two or more of the partners employing you (not encoded)
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment with the insolvent employer ended
      `my weekly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly rate of pay under your award, agreement or contract at the end of the employment, in dollars (the rate your leave, notice and redundancy pay are worked out at)
      `my unpaid annual leave` IS A NUMBER @desc What your award, agreement or contract entitles you to for annual leave accrued and not taken at the end of your employment, in dollars, before anything was paid towards it
      `my unpaid long service leave` IS A NUMBER @desc What you are entitled to for long service leave accrued (or pro rata) at the end of your employment, in dollars, before anything was paid towards it
      `my pay in lieu of notice` IS A NUMBER @desc What you are entitled to for a shortfall in your notice of termination, in dollars, before anything was paid towards it
      `my redundancy pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The redundancy pay you are entitled to, in dollars, before anything was paid towards it
      `the years of service my redundancy pay counts` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years of your service your redundancy pay is payable for: full years, plus a part year only if your award or agreement pays for part years
      `my wages entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc Your wages (including allowances, loadings, overtime and penalty rates) for work done or paid leave taken in the 13-week wages entitlement period, in dollars, before tax and before anything was paid towards it
      `the weeks I was employed in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of that 13-week period you were employed (13 if all of it; need not be a whole number)
      `my instrument set a rate for my regular work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your award, agreement or contract set a rate of pay, at the end of that period, for work you were expected to do regularly
      `that rate as a weekly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc That rate expressed as a weekly rate, in dollars (ignored if none)
      `the Secretary is satisfied there is no regular pattern` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary is satisfied that there was no regular pattern of your hours, or of your wages, over the weeks of that period (the Secretary's judgment)
      `the PAYG amount to be withheld from those wages` IS A NUMBER @desc The tax that must be withheld under PAYG from the wages counted, in dollars
      `already paid or payable for annual leave` IS A NUMBER @desc What anyone has paid you (or someone for your benefit) for the annual leave, or must pay you outside the winding up or bankruptcy, in dollars
      `already paid or payable for long service leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The same, for long service leave, in dollars
      `already paid or payable for notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The same, for pay in lieu of notice, in dollars
      `already paid or payable for redundancy` IS A NUMBER @desc The same, for redundancy pay, in dollars
      `already paid or payable for wages` IS A NUMBER @desc The same, for the wages in the 13-week period, in dollars
      `the day of the insolvency event` IS A DATE @desc The day the liquidator was appointed or your employer became bankrupt
      `a buyer of the business offered me the same work on terms no less favourable within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business was transferred (not to a bankruptcy trustee) and, within 14 days of your employment ending, the new owner offered you the same or substantially the same work on terms no less favourable overall
      `the buyer later made my job redundant or became insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that new owner then employed you and ended the job as no longer needed, or became insolvent and your job with them ended in connection with it
      `the Secretary has reduced it for my debts to my employer by` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount, in dollars, by which the Secretary has decided to reduce the advance because you owe your employer money (0 if none)
      `my debts to my employer` IS A NUMBER @desc The total you owe your employer, in dollars
      `the Secretary has reduced it to nil under s 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary, satisfied that the liquidator or trustee expects to have enough in the next 112 days to pay you in full, has reduced the advance to nil
GIVETH A `My advance with the maximum weekly wage worked out`
`How much is my advance with the maximum weekly wage worked out` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What maximum weekly wage caps my advance` `the day my employment ended`
    WHEN `the maximum weekly wage is` `w` THEN
        CONSIDER `How much is my advance` `I was employed for a partnership by two or more partners` `w` `my weekly rate` `my unpaid annual leave` `my unpaid long service leave` `my pay in lieu of notice` `my redundancy pay` `the years of service my redundancy pay counts` `my wages entitlement` `the weeks I was employed in the period` `my instrument set a rate for my regular work` `that rate as a weekly rate` `the Secretary is satisfied there is no regular pattern` `the PAYG amount to be withheld from those wages` `already paid or payable for annual leave` `already paid or payable for long service leave` `already paid or payable for notice` `already paid or payable for redundancy` `already paid or payable for wages` `the day of the insolvency event` `a buyer of the business offered me the same work on terms no less favourable within 14 days` `the buyer later made my job redundant or became insolvent` `the Secretary has reduced it for my debts to my employer by` `my debts to my employer` `the Secretary has reduced it to nil under s 18`
        WHEN `answered` `a` THEN `my advance is` `a`
        OTHERWISE `not covered: employment for a partnership by two or more of the partners is not encoded (s 10(2))`
    OTHERWISE `not covered: the maximum weekly wage for the year my employment ended is not worked out here`
